red list, add a ```` ```mermaid ```` `flowchart TD` adapted from the proposal's architecture flowchart. Nodes: Issue; Scanners (\"file issues\"); Triage (lead, engineer, optional roles); `plan.md`; \"Human `ard:approved` (when `require_approval`)\"; Worker (branch, tests, draft PR); Reviewers; Merger (\"reviews at head, checks green; protected paths need a human\"); Merged (issue closed); `ard:needs-human`. Edges: changes returns to the worker (\"review rounds, up to `max_review_rounds`\"); all approve gives \"PR ready\" to the merger; every stage has a dashed edge to `ard:needs-human`. Keep the numbered list. Confirm `max_review_rounds` and `require_approval` appear in `docs/site/configuration.md` or the proposal; use the exact names.\n\n### Test plan\n- `make docs-check` (runs `mkdocs build --strict -d /tmp/ard-site`, then `go test ./internal/docscheck/...`). It should pass with no broken-link warnings.\n- Check the built `/tmp/ard-site/index.html` contains `class=\"mermaid\"`.\n- Check the nav has Roles with five entries, and `grep -rn 'roles\\.md' docs/site README.md mkdocs.yml` returns nothing.\n- Failure case: if `CheckCommands` flags an invented command in the new pages, remove or correct it.\n- Edge case: relative links inside `roles/*.md` need `../` to reach other pages.\n- The worker's `make lint test` does not cover the docs build, so run `make docs-check` explicitly. It needs `mkdocs` (install with pip from `docs/site/requirements.txt`), and the worker has network access.\n\n### Risk\nLow. Docs and `mkdocs.yml` only; `mkdocs.yml` is not in `merge.protected_paths` and `.github/workflows/docs.yml` is untouched. A small rebase is possible against PR #401. The URL `roles.html` changes to `roles/`, so external links to the old page will break.\n\n### Size\nM (about 250 changed lines). Files: `mkdocs.yml`, `docs/site/index.md`, `docs/site/security.md`, `docs/site/roles.md` (deleted), and new `docs/site/roles/index.md`, `scanners.md`, `triage.md`, `workers.md` and `reviewers.md`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RscatTbVSd58qG8sJsJheq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
